{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The proposed side dormer by reason of its inappropriate\r\ndesign and prominent siting would be unsympathetic to, and fail to complement\r\nthe existing character of the original building, appearing as an incongruous\r\nfeature in the streetscene and resulting in undue harm to the character and\r\nappearance of the area. The proposed development would therefore be contrary to\r\nthe high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework\r\n(2023), Policies D3 D (1) and (11) of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1\r\n(B) of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policies DM 1 A, DM1 B (a), (b) (c) and\r\nDM26 A (g) of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and\r\nthe adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;The proposed first and second floor side\r\nextension due to the close proximity to Northumberland Road would appear as an\r\nunduly incongruous and dominant addition to the street scene.&amp;nbsp; The\r\nproposal would therefore be contrary to the high quality design of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3 D (1) and (11) of the London Plan\r\n(2021), Core Policy CS1 (B) of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), policy DM 1 A,\r\nDM1 B (a), (b) (c) and DM26 A (g) of the Harrow Development Management Policies\r\nLocal Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential\r\nDesign Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;In the absence of section drawings demonstrating\r\nsufficient floor to ceiling heights, it has not been demonstrated that the\r\nproposal would provide an acceptable standard of living accommodation for\r\nfuture occupiers to the detriment of their residential amenity. As such, the\r\nproposal is contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies\r\nD3.D(7) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1 of the Harrow Core Strategy\r\n(2013), and policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan\r\n(2013), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide\r\nSupplementary Planning Document (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
